            "type": "reasoning.summary",
            "summary": "**Clarifying storage process**\n\nI need to confirm that the new storage extension for the Effect Wednesday collection can be granted tomorrow. There's a deadline: if I save the 13:30 date today, can I change it for tomorrow's 13:45 reserve? For boxes already staged, the warehouse needs to act by 13:45. Unfortunately, a box missed on Monday is still in the cage. I can't assume the workflow will handle it automatically, so I'll need to communicate with the warehouse to ensure proper custody and secure the box overnight.**Addressing extension issues**\n\nI've been informed that the manager instructed for a full batch to be handled by 13:30, with no discretionary extensions available. We need to clarify that there's no record of date alterations and that unauthorized early actions can't be assumed. Every operator should follow the workflow policy; any outbound manifest needs to comply with this. I should explain that holding the manifest goes against routine release protocols. Additionally, if the manager can override, consistency in control is lost. I’ll also inform Claire that no actions should be suggested today, while asking if emergency authorization is a possibility.",
